<title>UK: UK Recycling Services Group to float on AIM at 90p.</title>
<headline>UK Recycling Services Group to float on AIM at 90p.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Recycling Services Group Plc, a metals handling and recycling group, said on Friday its shares will float on the London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market (AIM) at 90p.</p>
<p>The placing, by broker Albert E Sharp, will raise 3.6 million stg net and value the company at 14.6 million stg.</p>
<p>Proceeds of the float will partly go to finance the acquisition of G&amp;P Batteries Ltd for an initial 4.35 million stg, allowing the group to move into lead recycling.</p>
<p>Dealing in the shares will commence on November 28.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
</text>
